 by reading test pain signals — advisory only, no code changes. Use when tests are painful to write or maintain.</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.agents/skills/test-friction/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>ui-align</name>\n    <description>High-alignment UI specification workflow using interactive grilling and methodology verification. Use when specifying UI through interactive grilling.</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.agents/skills/ui-align/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>whisper</name>\n    <description>Deterministic knowledge workspace: session loop (recall all / append), scope routing, distill, bundle. Delegates to the turu CLI when installed; manual fallbacks otherwise.</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.agents/skills/whisper/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>wrap-up</name>\n    <description>End-of-day review across all projects. Synthesizes work-queue entries into the log, flags undocumented work. Trigger when the user says /wrap-up, &apos;end of day&apos;, &apos;day review&apos;, or &apos;daily close&apos;.</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.agents/skills/wrap-up/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>fck</name>\n    <description>Finish the sentence the user didn&apos;t write. Trigger when the user&apos;s message is primarily a swear — &quot;fuck&quot;, &quot;shit&quot;, &quot;oh shit&quot;, &quot;oh fuck&quot;, &quot;wtf&quot;, or elongated variants like &quot;fuuuuuk&quot; — instead of a description of a problem. Also for the explicit /fuck, /shit, /oh-shit, /oh-fuck, /fuuuuuk commands. The swear carries no content; the content is in what just happened on screen. Go look — last command, last edit, last error — and hand back a concrete diagnosis or the specific missing sentence, instead of asking &quot;what&apos;s wrong?&quot;, mirroring emotion, or lecturing about message quality. Extra repeated letters = more urgency (&quot;fuuuuuk&quot; vs &quot;fuck&quot;).</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.pi/agent/git/github.com/charly-vibes/fck/skills/fck/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>for-fucks-sake</name>\n    <description>Interview fallback when there is genuinely nothing in context to explain the user&apos;s frustration — no error, no recent edit, no obvious cause for a &quot;fuck&quot;/&quot;shit&quot;/&quot;wtf&quot;. Instead of guessing or asking an open-ended &quot;what&apos;s wrong?&quot;, ask exactly one question at a time, each with a best-guess answer attached so the user can confirm in one word. Also invoked directly as /for-fucks-sake.</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.pi/agent/git/github.com/charly-vibes/fck/skills/for-fucks-sake/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>no-shit</name>\n    <description>Verification pass before calling any fix &quot;done&quot; — especially incident-tier fixes (/oh-shit, /oh-fuck, intensity 4-5). Check real output instead of trusting that the change was made, scan once for side effects, then state the verdict plainly. Use after applying any fix whose failure would matter, or when invoked directly as /no-shit. Replaces the one-shot &quot;fixed it&quot; claim with actual confirmation, stopping the moment it&apos;s genuinely confirmed.</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.pi/agent/git/github.com/charly-vibes/fck/skills/no-shit/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>would-you-please-fucking-stop</name>\n    <description>Circuit-breaker for when the agent itself is the problem — looping on the same failed fix, hedging, restating the same answer without new information, or producing repetition instead of progress. Named after Ursula K. Le Guin&apos;s essay &quot;Would You Please Fucking Stop?&quot;. Use when frustration is aimed at how the conversation is going rather than at the task. Forces a reset to actual current state and exactly one concrete next step. Also invoked directly as /would-you-please-fucking-stop.</description>\n    <location>/var/home/sasha/.pi/agent/git/github.com/charly-vibes/fck/skills/would-you-please-fucking-stop/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n</available_skills>\n</skills>","cwd":"<cwd>\n/var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina\n</cwd>"},"timestamp":1792525762414,"toolsAdded":[{"name":"read","description":"Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)"},"offset":{"type":"number","description":"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of lines to read"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"bash","description":"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["command"],"properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"Shell command to execute"},"timeout":{"type":"number","description":"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"edit","description":"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","edits"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["oldText","newText"],"properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call."},"newText":{"type":"string","description":"Replacement text for this targeted edit."}}},"description":"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead."}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"write","description":"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","content"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)"},"content":{"type":"string","description":"Content to write to the file"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"ah_check","description":"Validate spec-test correspondence for the espectacular setup in the project: checks every deployed spec scenario against its contract TOML and, with run_tests, executes the declared contract tests. Prefer this over running `ah check` via bash — it returns the structured JSON envelope. Exit code 1 means findings exist.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"changes":{"type":"string","description":"In-flight openspec change name to validate with (change overlay)"},"project":{"type":"string","description":"Project root directory (defaults to the session working directory)"},"run_tests":{"type":"boolean","description":"Also execute declared contract tests (slower; default false)"}}}},{"name":"ah_doctor","description":"Diagnose the espectacular setup in the project: config, version drift, specs/changes dirs, managed blocks, hooks, and framework recommendations. Read-only.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"project":{"type":"string","description":"Project root directory (defaults to the session working directory)"}}}},{"name":"ah_signals","description":"Emit dont drift signals from the espectacular setup in the project. Read-only.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"project":{"type":"string","description":"Project root directory (defaults to the session working directory)"}}}},{"name":"ah_explain","description":"Playbook guidance for an espectacular finding kind, suggested action, or topic (e.g. no-tests-declared, contract-stale, workflow, scenario-scoped-tests). Returns the full guidance text.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["topic"],"properties":{"topic":{"type":"string","description":"Finding kind, suggested action, or topic slug"},"project":{"type":"string","description":"Project root directory (defaults to the session working directory)"}}}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are the implementor subagent for ticket evallerina-fok (lane afk).\n\nRead first: .wai/projects/evallerina/briefs/evallerina-fok.md — it is your\ncomplete specification (desired outcome, exact files, red/green sequence,\nanti-goals, follow-up threshold).\n\nWorking dir: this repo (evallerina). Work ONLY here; do not touch sibling repos.\n\nMethod: strict TDD per the brief's red/green sequence — write the failing\ntest, run it (RED), implement (GREEN), then tidy. Commit at each green step\nwith conventional messages referencing evallerina-fok.\n\nGates before you finish (all must be green):\n- cargo test\n- just tier0\n- dogfood: cargo run -- doc-audit → non-empty inventory, zero silent skips\n\nCompletion criteria: the brief's commands exit 0 and tasks 2.1–2.5 in\nopenspec/changes/add-ecosystem-doc-evals/tasks.md are checked off.\n\nStop conditions (STOP and record in your final message, do not thrash):\n- any red test unresolved after 2 attempts\n- real-ecosystem audit rows exceed ~40 or a real tool's --help resists\n  parsing >1h (follow-up threshold in brief)\n\nWhen done: commit everything, and end with a final summary message listing\ncommits, test results verbatim tail, and openspec tasks checked."}],"timestamp":1792525762413},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-2b4b64a1-d767-41bc-8cde-bf7a6491a9d2","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cat /var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina/.wai/projects/evallerina/briefs/evallerina-fok.md","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":11154,"output":54,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":11208,"cost":{"input":0.0016730999999999998,"output":0.000027,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0017000999999999997}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792525762422,"responseId":"gen-1792525762-zho0Fko8QGXG9tuwhaZc","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-2b4b64a1-d767-41bc-8cde-bf7a6491a9d2","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Brief: evallerina-fok — tier-0 doc-coverage audit\n\nTicket: evallerina-fok (P2, complexity:l, lane:afk). Implement the tier-0\ndoc-coverage audit (surface extractor + inventory scanner + audit rows), per\nopenspec change `add-ecosystem-doc-evals` (tasks 2.1–2.5, design D1/D4).\n\n## Why\nBounded pure-Rust module with a crisp TDD shape (harvest tokens → scan docs →\nemit rows) but large breadth: two extractors, a config format, and report\nwiring. Delegation keeps the lead session lean for orchestrating the rest of\nthe epic (phases 3–6 depend on this landing). Independent value: after this\nlands, `just tier0` flags undocumented or unfindable features across the\necosystem the moment docs drift.\n\n## Desired outcome\nNew `src/doc_audit.rs` (Purpose/Responsibilities/Rationale header — e10 Must\ngate) providing:\n1. **Surface extractor** — runs a tool's binary with `--help` (subprocess,\n   in a provisioned fixture sandbox for tests) and harvests a feature-token\n   set: subcommands, long flags, and documented exit codes where `--help`\n   lists them. Token normalization: kebab/snake/spacing variants treated as\n   equivalent (substring-normalized matching per D1).\n2. **Inventory scanner** — scans a repo's docs surfaces (`README.md`,\n   `docs/**`, `llms.txt`, `AGENTS.md` managed blocks) into per-surface\n   feature-token sets.\n3. **Breadcrumb reachability** — a token found in docs but NOT reachable\n   from `llms.txt` or managed-block breadcrumbs → `ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE`; a\n   token absent from all surfaces → `ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED`.\n4. **Config** — a checked-in `doc_audit.toml` (tool → repo path, binary\n   name, optional `surface = \"none\"`); `surface: none` tools (e.g. `bd`,\n   `openspec` — not Rust CLIs) skip the binary step and are recorded in\n   provenance, never silently skipped. Absent binaries record provenance\n   `binary_absent` (never silent skip).\n5. **Report wiring** — audit rows flow into the existing report as new\n   check-codes `ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED` / `ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE`;\n   `report_version` stays 1 (additive); `tests/report_aggregation.rs`\n   expectations pass unchanged.\n6. CLI: `evallerina doc-audit` subcommand; wired into `just tier0`.\n\n## Exact files\n- NEW `src/doc_audit.rs` — extractors + scanner + audit rows (MUST carry\n  Purpose header)\n- NEW `doc_audit.toml` — per-tool audit config (all routing.toml tools)\n- `src/lib.rs` — module registration\n- `src/main.rs` — `doc-audit` subcommand + tier-0 wiring\n- `src/report.rs` — accept the two new check-codes (additive only)\n- NEW `tests/doc_audit.rs` — surface + inventory contract tests (failing\n  first); fixture binaries are throwaway shell scripts in a temp dir, NOT\n  real ecosystem binaries\n\n## Red/green sequence\n1. RED: surface test — fixture script prints a `--help` with 2 subcommands +\n   long flags → harvested token set matches, with a kebab/snake pair\n   normalizing to one token. GREEN.\n2. RED: `surface: none` test — tool declared `surface: none` produces no\n   binary probe and records `skip` in provenance. GREEN.\n3. RED: inventory test — fixture repo (temp dir: README + docs/x.md +\n   llms.txt + AGENTS.md managed block) → per-surface token sets. GREEN.\n4. RED: reachability test — token in `docs/x.md` not referenced by\n   `llms.txt`/managed block → `ERR_DOC_NOT_FINDABLE`; token absent\n   everywhere → `ERR_FEATURE_UNDOCUMENTED`; token reachable → no row. GREEN.\n5. RED: `binary_absent` test — configured binary missing → provenance\n   `binary_absent`, loud, not silent. GREEN.\n6. Wire report rows (additive) + CLI + `doc_audit.toml` for the real\n   ecosystem; `just tier0` green. Dogfood check (meter): audit run against\n   evallerina's own surfaces produces a non-empty inventory with zero\n   silent skips.\n\n## Out of scope\n- No routing/filing changes (e4x owns routing audit faults)\n- No new scenario families or tier-2 recordings (vrr/t7n)\n- No report_version bump, no aggregate doc-quality score (anti-goal)\n- No edits to any sibling repo's docs\n\n## Anti-goals\n- Never silently skip a source: every skip is provenance (`skip`,\n  `binary_absent`) — pinned by test\n- No aggregate score field (pinned by test, same discipline as 48g)\n- Token normalization must NOT be tuned to pass evallerina's own docs only\n  (general normalization rules only)\n\n## Commands\n- `cargo test` per red/green step; `just tier0` at end; dogfood:\n  `cargo run -- doc-audit` against evallerina itself → non-empty inventory,\n  zero silent skips\n\n## Follow-up threshold\nIf real-ecosystem audit rows exceed ~40 or the `--help` parsing of any real\ntool resists the extractor (>1h), STOP: record findings as research, ship\nthe mechanism against fixtures, and leave real-tool onboarding notes for\n73q (validation phase). Do not tune normalization to make real rows vanish.\n\n## Verifier evidence contract\nThe verify session's review artifact MUST cite the artifacts it read and\ninclude fresh `cargo test doc_audit` + `just tier0` output before recording\nCONFIRM — otherwise REVIEW_REQUIRED.\n\n## Spawn model\nImplementor: `openrouter/z-ai/glm-5.3-flash` (matches PI_PROVIDER default);\ncontext ceiling ≤ 50% of its window, computed at spawn.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792525764816},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me explore the repo structure first.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Let me explore the repo structure first.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-386eff01-d74d-4fa6-b95c-aeb344e401c3","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina && ls && ls src tests 2>/dev/null && cat Cargo.toml | head -40 && cat justfile 2>/dev/null | head -60","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":12547,"output":77,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":10,"totalTokens":12624,"cost":{"input":0.00188205,"output":0.0000385,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0019205499999999998}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792525764819,"responseId":"gen-1792525764-MzLkloFztqaEGW3sbdJq","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-386eff01-d74d-4fa6-b95c-aeb344e401c3","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"AGENTS.md\nCargo.lock\nCargo.toml\nCLAUDE.md\ndocs\nfixtures\njustfile\nopenspec\nREADME.md\nrouting.toml\nscenarios\nsrc\ntarget\ntests\n_typos.toml\nsrc:\nablation.rs\nenvelope.rs\nlib.rs\nlive.rs\nmain.rs\nrecorded.rs\nregistry.rs\nreport.rs\nrouting_parity.rs\nrouting.rs\nscenario.rs\n\ntests:\nablate_cli.rs\nablation.rs\nevals_replay.rs\nlive_protocol.rs\nreport_aggregation.rs\nrouting_parity.rs\nrouting.rs\n[package]\nname = \"evallerina\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2024\"\ndescription = \"Eval battery for the dulce-de-leche tool family: do LLM agents actually use the suite's AIX output channels?\"\nlicense = \"Apache-2.0\"\nrepository = \"https://github.com/charly-vibes/evallerina\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\n\n[lib]\nname = \"evallerina\"\n\n[[bin]]\nname = \"evallerina\"\npath = \"src/main.rs\"\n\n[dependencies]\ngenesis-vibes = { git = \"https://github.com/charly-vibes/genesis\", tag = \"v0.12.3\" }\nclap = { version = \"4\", features = [\"derive\", \"env\"] }\nserde = { version = \"1\", features = [\"derive\"] }\nserde_json = \"1\"\ntoml = \"0.8\"\nregex = \"1\"\nthiserror = \"2\"\nureq = { version = \"2\", default-features = false, features = [\"tls\", \"json\"] }\n# evallerina — eval battery for the dulce-de-leche tool family\n# Tier ladder per genesis evals-guidelines: 0 static (push) / 1 replay (nightly) / 2 live (scheduled)\n\ndefault:\n    @just --list\n\n# Tier 0 — static checks, no model (gates every push)\ntier0:\n    cargo fmt --check\n    cargo clippy -- -D warnings\n    cargo test\n\n# Tier 1 — scripted replay of recorded AgentStep transcripts, no model, no network\ntier1:\n    cargo test --test evals_replay -- --nocapture\n\n# Tier 2 — live rotation (requires OPENROUTER_API_KEY); never gates a push.\n# One JSON event per cell on stdout (trial row or absent record).\ntier2 model=\"openrouter/free\" scenario=\"\" budget=\"20\":\n    #!/usr/bin/env bash\n    set -euo pipefail\n    args=(live --model \"{{model}}\" --budget-mins \"{{budget}}\")\n    if [ -n \"{{scenario}}\" ]; then args+=(\"{{scenario}}\"); fi\n    cargo run --release -- \"${args[@]}\"\n\n# Build + test the harness crate\nci: tier0\n\n# Fixture sandbox smoke test: provision binaries, run one replay scenario\nsmoke:\n    cargo run --release -- smoke\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792525767798},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-2c926ec5-d8cc-4dc4-bd75-1f28f2d67a53","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina && cat src/lib.rs && cat src/report.rs | head -120","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":13261,"output":50,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":13311,"cost":{"input":0.00198915,"output":0.000024999999999999998,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0020141499999999997}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792525767799,"responseId":"gen-1792525767-HaEN8EURtZqWPSjUMHqJ","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-2c926ec5-d8cc-4dc4-bd75-1f28f2d67a53","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"//! Purpose: Library core of the evallerina harness — the consumer eval\n//! battery for the dulce-de-leche tool family (wai first, most adopted).\n//! Responsibilities: parse the family's envelope channels (which drift\n//! from genesis's generic `hints` shape), load recorded agent\n//! trajectories from `scenarios/`, and assemble tier-1 replay scenarios\n//! with deterministic checks from `genesis::evals`.\n//! Rationale: process-boundary scoring per the genesis evals-guidelines\n//! spec — the harness only ever asserts on captured stdout/stderr, exit\n//! codes, and fixture state; free-form agent text is never scored. The\n//! dulce-specific envelope readers live here because the reusable\n//! genesis helpers assume a top-level `hints` array, while real tool\n//! output (wai 2026.10.5) carries remediation under `data.remediation`.\n\npub mod ablation;\npub mod envelope;\npub mod live;\npub mod recorded;\npub mod registry;\npub mod report;\npub mod routing;\npub mod routing_parity;\npub mod scenario;\n//! Purpose: Tier-1/2 report aggregation into the per-channel fault\n//! dashboard (evallerina-48g).\n//! Responsibilities: aggregate report_version 1 rows (tier-2 rotation\n//! events and tier-1 rows without model attribution) into a\n//! per-output-channel × check-code × model-id fault matrix, apply the\n//! evals-guidelines fault routing (tool faults → tool tickets; agent\n//! faults → AIX-channel work only at the cross-model threshold),\n//! surface absent, rate_limited, and http_error cells as coverage\n//! records — never failures, never dropped — and refuse loudly on unmappable scenarios\n//! instead of silently bucketing them.\n//! Rationale: evals-guidelines \"Fault routing\" and \"suite-wide\n//! aggregation\" requirements. The dashboard deliberately carries no\n//! single aggregate score: per-capability breakdown is a hard\n//! requirement, and a collapse into one number hides exactly the\n//! channel × code × model signal the routing rule needs.\n\nuse serde_json::json;\nuse std::collections::{BTreeMap, BTreeSet};\n\n/// Validate the `report` subcommand's routing flags: `--file` (cross-repo\n/// write authorization, Phase 2) requires `--route` — filing proposed\n/// tickets only makes sense after the routing step ran. Any combination\n/// without `--file` is fine.\npub fn validate_route_flags(route: bool, file: bool) -> Result<(), String> {\n    if file && !route {\n        return Err(\n            \"--file requires --route: filing proposed tickets only makes sense after the routing step ran\".into(),\n        );\n    }\n    Ok(())\n}\n\n/// The scenario definition's recorded tool — the repo key for routing\n/// (routing.rs keys proposals on this, never the report row's `tool`\n/// field, which is hardcoded for live trials). Scenario names\n/// prefix-encode the eval target by convention (`wai-*`, `dont-*`);\n/// an unknown prefix is None → a loud error downstream (never a\n/// silent bucket, mirroring aggregate_rows).\npub fn scenario_tool_of(name: &str) -> Option<String> {\n    if name.starts_with(\"wai-\") {\n        Some(\"wai\".to_owned())\n    } else if name.starts_with(\"dont-\") {\n        Some(\"dont\".to_owned())\n    } else {\n        None\n    }\n}\n\n/// Run the routing step against an aggregated dashboard: propose\n/// dry-run tickets from the same rows the dashboard aggregated from,\n/// optionally file them (Phase 2, `--file`), and attach the additive\n/// `routed` summary — decision counts only, no aggregate score — to\n/// the dashboard JSON.\n///\n/// Returns the proposals so the caller can serialize\n/// proposed-tickets.jsonl. Routing never affects the exit code unless\n/// it errors loudly (empty registry, unknown scenario, version\n/// mismatch): skipped proposals (unmapped tool, bd failure) are the\n/// record, not failures.\npub fn attach_routing(\n    dashboard: &mut serde_json::Value,\n    rows: &[serde_json::Value],\n    configured_models: &[String],\n    repo_map: &BTreeMap<String, String>,\n    file_authorized: bool,\n    run_bd: &mut crate::routing::BdRunner,\n) -> Result<Vec<crate::routing::ProposalRow>, String> {\n    let mut proposals =\n        crate::routing::propose(rows, configured_models, &scenario_tool_of, repo_map)?;\n    crate::routing::file_proposals(&mut proposals, file_authorized, run_bd)?;\n\n    let (mut filed, mut existing, mut dry_run, mut skipped) = (0usize, 0, 0, 0);\n    for p in &proposals {\n        match p.decision.as_str() {\n            \"filed\" => filed += 1,\n            \"existing\" => existing += 1,\n            \"dry_run\" => dry_run += 1,\n            _ => skipped += 1,\n        }\n    }\n    dashboard[\"routed\"] = json!({\n        \"filed\": filed,\n        \"existing\": existing,\n        \"dry_run\": dry_run,\n        \"skipped\": skipped,\n    });\n    Ok(proposals)\n}\n\n/// The full CLI routing step for `report --route`: load routing.toml\n/// (from the current directory — the repo root on rotation day),\n/// attach the routed summary to the dashboard, and write\n/// proposed-tickets.jsonl next to the report file. `file_authorized`\n/// comes from the explicit `--file` flag; the runner is injectable so\n/// tests can spy on bd calls.\npub fn run_routing_step(\n    dashboard: &mut serde_json::Value,\n    rows: &[serde_json::Value],\n    configured_models: &[String],\n    report_path: &std::path::Path,\n    file_authorized: bool,\n    run_bd: &mut crate::routing::BdRunner,\n) -> Result<Vec<crate::routing::ProposalRow>, String> {\n    let content = std::fs::read_to_string(\"routing.toml\")\n        .map_err(|e| format!(\"cannot read routing.toml: {e}\"))?;\n    let repo_map = crate::routing::parse_routing_toml(&content)?;\n    let proposals = attach_routing(\n        dashboard,\n        rows,\n        configured_models,\n        &repo_map,\n        file_authorized,\n        run_bd,\n    )?;\n    let jsonl = crate::routing::to_jsonl(&proposals);\n    let out_path = report_path\n        .parent()\n        .unwrap_or(std::path::Path::new(\".\"))\n        .join(\"proposed-tickets.jsonl\");\n    std::fs::write(&out_path, jsonl)\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792525770068},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-2e2741e4-fe79-469d-91fd-e79e969f1406","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /var/home/sasha/para/areas/dev/gh/charly/evallerina && sed -n '120,260p' src/report.rs && echo ==== && cat src/main.rs | head -150","timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":14750,"output":61,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":14811,"cost":{"input":0.0022125,"output":0.0000305,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.002243}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792525770070,"responseId":"gen-1792525770-ocsso6G2zpruBZRcsu1l","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-2e2741e4-fe79-469d-91fd-e79e969f1406","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"    std::fs::write(&out_path, jsonl)\n        .map_err(|e| format!(\"cannot write {}: {e}\", out_path.display()))?;\n    Ok(proposals)\n}\n\n/// Version of the dashboard shape. Additive evolution only within a\n/// version; breaking changes bump this.\npub const DASHBOARD_VERSION: u32 = 1;\n\n/// The evals-guidelines cross-model routing threshold for agent faults\n/// within one output channel.\nconst ROUTING_THRESHOLD: usize = 3;\n\n/// The output channel a live scenario's checks probe (the fault-routing\n/// key per evals-guidelines: suggestions, envelope, managed-block, or\n/// artifact surface). Registered for every live scenario; the channel\n/// must exist before rotation day, not after the first dashboard run.\npub fn scenario_channel(name: &str) -> Option<&'static str> {\n    match name {\n        \"wai-hint-adherence-smoke\"\n        | \"wai-hint-adherence-corrupt-config\"\n        | \"dont-hint-adherence-lifecycle\" => Some(\"envelope\"),\n        \"wai-hint-adherence-typo\" => Some(\"suggestions\"),\n        \"wai-doc-drift-stale-agents-md\" | \"dont-doc-drift-stale-lifecycle\" => Some(\"artifact\"),\n        // Archetype family (evallerina-bhh): vampiro-polyglot-seam asserts\n        // on vampiro's gate/guidance JSON envelopes; wai-drifted-ecosystem\n        // probes the stale-AGENTS.md artifact via doc_drift_blindness,\n        // mapping to `artifact` like its doc-drift siblings.\n        \"vampiro-polyglot-seam\" => Some(\"envelope\"),\n        \"wai-drifted-ecosystem\" => Some(\"artifact\"),\n        _ => None,\n    }\n}\n\n/// One accumulator key in the routing maps: agent faults key on\n/// (channel, code), tool faults on (tool, check, channel) because they\n/// carry no code by contract.\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq, PartialOrd, Ord)]\nenum FaultKey {\n    /// Agent fault: the `ERR_*` taxonomy code within one output channel.\n    Agent { channel: String, code: String },\n    /// Tool fault: no code; routed to the tool's repository.\n    Tool {\n        tool: String,\n        check: String,\n        channel: String,\n    },\n}\n\n/// Accumulated occurrences for one fault key: total count plus the set\n/// of distinct model ids observed (empty for non-tier-2 rows).\n#[derive(Debug, Default)]\nstruct FaultTally {\n    occurrences: usize,\n    models: BTreeSet<String>,\n    scenarios: BTreeSet<String>,\n}\n\n/// Aggregate report_version 1 rows into the dashboard JSON.\n///\n/// `rows` are parsed report rows as [`serde_json::Value`]: tier-2\n/// rotation events (`kind: trial | absent`) or tier-1 rows without a\n/// `model` field (grouped as non-tier-2 per the report contract).\n/// `configured_models` is the model registry the rotation was\n/// configured with — it defines the routing threshold (3, or the full\n/// registry size when fewer than three are configured). `channel_of`\n/// resolves a scenario to the output channel its checks probe; an\n/// unknown scenario is a loud error, never a silent bucket.\n///\n/// The returned value is the serialized dashboard shape: no single\n/// aggregate score, per-capability breakdown only.\npub fn aggregate_rows(\n    rows: &[serde_json::Value],\n    configured_models: &[String],\n    channel_of: &dyn Fn(&str) -> Option<&'static str>,\n) -> Result<serde_json::Value, String> {\n    if configured_models.is_empty() {\n        return Err(\"configured model registry is empty — no routing threshold exists\".into());\n    }\n    let routing_threshold = configured_models.len().min(ROUTING_THRESHOLD);\n\n    let mut matrix_cells: BTreeMap<(String, String, String), FaultTally> = BTreeMap::new();\n    let mut routings: BTreeMap<FaultKey, FaultTally> = BTreeMap::new();\n    let mut coverage = Coverage::default();\n    let mut report_versions = BTreeSet::new();\n\n    for row in rows {\n        let kind = row.get(\"kind\").and_then(serde_json::Value::as_str);\n        if kind == Some(\"absent\") {\n            // Absent cells are the record that a cell did not run; they\n            // are never failures and never dropped (anti-goal).\n            coverage.absent += 1;\n            continue;\n        }\n        let status = row\n            .get(\"status\")\n            .and_then(serde_json::Value::as_str)\n            .ok_or(\"report row lacks a `status` field\")?;\n        let scenario = row\n            .get(\"scenario\")\n            .and_then(serde_json::Value::as_str)\n            .ok_or(\"report row lacks a `scenario` field\")?;\n        let tool = row\n            .get(\"tool\")\n            .and_then(serde_json::Value::as_str)\n            .ok_or(\"report row lacks a `tool` field\")?;\n        let checks = row\n            .get(\"checks\")\n            .and_then(serde_json::Value::as_array)\n            .ok_or(\"report row lacks a `checks` array\")?;\n        let report_version = row\n            .get(\"report_version\")\n            .and_then(serde_json::Value::as_u64)\n            .ok_or(\"report row lacks a `report_version` field\")?;\n        if report_version != 1 {\n            return Err(format!(\n                \"report row carries report_version {report_version}; this dashboard aggregates version 1 only\"\n            ));\n        }\n        report_versions.insert(report_version);\n\n        let channel = channel_of(scenario).ok_or_else(|| {\n            format!(\"scenario '{scenario}' has no declared output channel — refusing to aggregate\")\n        })?;\n\n        let model = row.get(\"model\").and_then(serde_json::Value::as_str);\n        match model {\n            Some(_) => {\n                coverage.trials += 1;\n                bump_status(&mut coverage, status)?;\n            }\n            None => coverage.non_tier2 += 1,\n        }\n\n        for check in checks {\n            let name = check\n                .get(\"name\")\n                .and_then(serde_json::Value::as_str)\n                .ok_or(\"check row lacks a `name` field\")?;\n            let passed = check\n                .get(\"passed\")\n====\n//! Purpose: CLI entry point of the evallerina harness.\n//! Responsibilities: expose the tier commands the justfile recipes\n//! invoke — `smoke` (run the replay smoke scenario, exit code carries\n//! pass/fail) and `live` (tier-2 live rotation over scenario × model\n//! cells via the OpenRouter :free action protocol).\n//! Rationale: tier discipline — the binary gates tier-0/1 locally and\n//! in CI; tier-2 never gates a push. `live` prints one JSON event per\n//! cell (trial row or absent record) and exits nonzero only when a\n//! trial actually failed or malformed — skipped cells are the record.\n\nuse std::io::Write;\nuse std::process::ExitCode;\nuse std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n\nuse clap::{Parser, Subcommand};\nuse evallerina::ablation::{\n    AblationFactories, AixArtifacts, AixSource, ToolBinaries, run_ablation,\n};\nuse evallerina::live::{OpenRouterTransport, RotationEvent, TrialStatus, run_rotation};\nuse evallerina::recorded::RecordedTrajectory;\nuse evallerina::registry::{DEFAULT_REPETITIONS, ordered_ids};\nuse evallerina::scenario::{SCENARIOS_DIR, live_scenario_by_name, live_scenarios, smoke_scenario};\n\n/// Default per-run wall-clock budget for the live rotation, minutes.\nconst DEFAULT_BUDGET_MINS: u64 = 20;\n\n/// Evals with an avatar — measuring whether agents actually use the tools.\n#[derive(Parser)]\n#[command(name = \"evallerina\", version, about)]\nstruct Cli {\n    #[command(subcommand)]\n    command: Command,\n}\n\n#[derive(Subcommand)]\nenum Command {\n    /// Run the tier-1 smoke replay (no model, no network). Exit 0 iff green.\n    Smoke,\n    /// Tier-2 live rotation (requires OPENROUTER_API_KEY). One JSON\n    /// event per cell on stdout: a report_version 1 trial row, or an\n    /// absent record when the per-run budget skipped the cell.\n    Live {\n        /// Optional scenario name filter (default: the whole live battery).\n        #[arg(default_value = None)]\n        scenario: Option<String>,\n        /// Repetitions per scenario × model cell.\n        #[arg(long, default_value_t = DEFAULT_REPETITIONS)]\n        reps: u32,\n        /// Run only this model id (default: the whole registry, in order).\n        #[arg(long, default_value = None)]\n        model: Option<String>,\n        /// Per-run wall-clock budget, minutes; cells not started before\n        /// it expires are recorded absent, never failed.\n        #[arg(long, default_value_t = DEFAULT_BUDGET_MINS)]\n        budget_mins: u64,\n    },\n    /// A/B ablation over one scenario (evals.md Step 5): the full arm\n    /// (AIX artifacts provisioned) vs the ablated arm (raw binaries),\n    /// ≥3 runs per arm over the configured model registry. Writes the\n    /// per-arm rotation rows as ArmReport JSONL to --out and prints the\n    /// per-arm summary + delta as JSON on stdout.\n    Ablate {\n        /// Scenario name (a live battery scenario; unknown names are a\n        /// loud error).\n        scenario: String,\n        /// Repetitions per arm (the evals.md Step 5 delta floor is 3).\n        #[arg(long, default_value_t = DEFAULT_REPETITIONS)]\n        reps: u32,\n        /// Run only this model id (default: the whole registry, in order).\n        #[arg(long, default_value = None)]\n        model: Option<String>,\n        /// Dry-run: every cell is recorded absent — no model calls, no\n        /// network; exercises the full report path hermetically.\n        #[arg(long)]\n        dry_run: bool,\n        /// Real artifact generation (opt-in; evallerina-0j8): invoke the\n        /// provisioned `wai` binary and harvest what it produces for the\n        /// full arm, instead of the static hermetic contents. A tool\n        /// failure is a loud error, never a placeholder fallback.\n        #[arg(long)]\n        real_artifacts: bool,\n        /// Per-run wall-clock budget, minutes; cells not started before\n        /// it expires are recorded absent, never failed.\n        #[arg(long, default_value_t = DEFAULT_BUDGET_MINS)]\n        budget_mins: u64,\n        /// Path the ArmReport JSONL rows are written to (full arm rows\n        /// first, then ablated, in run order).\n        #[arg(long)]\n        out: String,\n    },\n    /// Aggregate report rows (one JSON value per line in a JSONL file —\n    /// tier-2 rotation events or tier-1 rows) into the per-channel\n    /// fault dashboard. Prints the dashboard JSON to stdout; exits\n    /// nonzero on aggregation errors (unknown scenario, version\n    /// mismatch), never on fault findings.\n    Report {\n        /// Path to the JSONL report rows to aggregate.\n        path: String,\n        /// Run the fault-routing step after aggregation (dry-run by\n        /// default): attach the additive `routed` summary to the\n        /// dashboard and write proposed-tickets.jsonl next to the report.\n        #[arg(long)]\n        route: bool,\n        /// File the proposed tickets in their mapped repositories\n        /// (explicit cross-repo write authorization, Phase 2).\n        /// Requires --route.\n        #[arg(long)]\n        file: bool,\n    },\n    /// Tier-0 routing-map parity gate (evallerina-0sy): diff\n    /// routing.toml against dulce-de-leche's MANAGED-TOOLS block\n    /// (../dulce-de-leche/README.md). Prints the parity report as JSON\n    /// (degraded flag + one row per managed tool) and exits nonzero iff\n    /// any row failed; an absent ddl sibling degrades to a warning row\n    /// with exit 0 (standalone clones), never covering a parse failure.\n    RoutingParity,\n}\n\n/// The hermetic static artifact set the full arm provisions by default\n/// (the ablated-arm baseline stays raw binaries either way). Real\n/// generation — the provisioned `wai` binary harvesting the actual\n/// managed AGENTS.md, `.genesis/tools.toml` and `llms.txt` — is opt-in\n/// via --real-artifacts (evallerina-0j8).\nconst DEFAULT_AIX_ARTIFACTS: AixArtifacts = AixArtifacts {\n    llms_txt: \"llms.txt content: wai status --json\",\n    managed_agents_md: \"<!-- WAI:START -->managed guidance<!-- WAI:END -->\",\n    tools_toml: \"[tools]\\nwai = { cmd = \\\"wai\\\" }\\n\",\n};\n\nfn main() -> std::process::ExitCode {\n    match Cli::parse().command {\n        Command::Smoke => {\n            let path = std::path::Path::new(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\"))\n                .join(SCENARIOS_DIR)\n                .join(\"wai-hint-adherence-smoke.json\");\n            let content = std::fs::read_to_string(&path)\n                .unwrap_or_else(|e| panic!(\"read {}: {e}\", path.display()));\n            let trajectory = RecordedTrajectory::from_json(&content)\n                .unwrap_or_else(|e| panic!(\"parse {}: {e}\", path.display()));\n            let report = smoke_scenario()\n                .run(trajectory.steps())\n                .unwrap_or_else(|e| panic!(\"replay failed: {e}\"));\n            println!(\"{}\", serde_json::to_string_pretty(&report).unwrap());\n            if report.passed {\n                ExitCode::SUCCESS\n            } else {\n                ExitCode::FAILURE\n            }\n        }\n        Command::Live {\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792525771547},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[thinking-loop-guard: removed 44 chars of degenerate repetition — 'lock' ×11; generation was looping. Reason about the task from the earlier context.]"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"aborted","timestamp":1792525771549,"responseId":"gen-1792525771-5tU3APSDeEEUEYvcmWx4","errorMessage":"Request was aborted"}],"willRetry":false}
